  "releaseNotes": "Widens the LC006 doc (~95 lines) to spell out the AsSplitQuery() tradeoff (extra roundtrips, per-statement plan cost, snapshot consistency, transaction scope), when Cartesian is legitimately the right call, and the rule boundary against LC028 (depth) and LC038 (count). Adds a lock-in test that two sibling reference navigations stay quiet because reference navigations cannot Cartesian-inflate. Tests-only release; no analyzer or fixer behaviour change.",
